From 76d37578c69d670eabe868f4a8d908c39ec73f76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:12:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: WebGL uniform uploads from an empty array are
 INVALID_VALUE

uniform*v and uniformMatrix*fv took an empty array as a count of 0 and recorded it; the executor's replay checks the
data size against the count and stopped the engine on uniformMatrix2fv(loc, false, []). Chrome reports INVALID_VALUE
for an array shorter than one element, as the multiple-of-size check already did for the rest.
---
 .../WebGL/WebGL2RenderingContextImpl.cpp      | 22 +++++++++-------
 .../WebGL/WebGL2RenderingContextOverloads.cpp | 26 ++++++++++++-------
 .../WebGL/WebGLRenderingContextOverloads.cpp  | 26 ++++++++++++-------
 3 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/WebGL/WebGL2RenderingContextImpl.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/WebGL/WebGL2RenderingContextImpl.cpp
index 06f1bd8833..b7ad424fe2 100644
